nodecode-telnyx is a rewrite of team-telnyx's team-telnyx/hermes-inference-provider:
https://github.com/team-telnyx/hermes-inference-provider
commit f53c20e80f84b4a880a7f2b4f1ed2f8b3fa1d11c
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Telnyx LLC (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the provider profile itself — its name and description, its base of
https://api.telnyx.com/v2/ai/openai, the TELNYX_API_KEY variable and key page,
its curated fallback model list (models.json here), and its rules that no
output cap is volunteered, because a cap beside function tools trips Telnyx
error 10015 on hosted models — as a Nodecode catalog row and a credential hook;
the live catalog the profile fetched itself is now the core's own listing of
any catalog provider, which already sends the lane's Bearer key.

Left out, and why: the profile's own fetch_models and its hermes-cli user
agent (the core's listing replaces both), its task filter on the catalog
rows (Telnyx currently lists chat models only, and the core's listing keeps
ids, display names, windows and owners rather than task labels), and the per-1M
price normalization (the core's listing reads no rates, so the bundled rows
carry no cost rather than a guessed one). Its default auxiliary model has no
per-provider home in Nodecode, so it is not carried over. The two private host
imports the original needs — hermes_cli.__version__ and
hermes_cli.urllib_security — have no place here.
